    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Variceal bleeding: endoscopic banding plus IV octreotide (somatostatin analog; bolus, then infusion for 3-5 days after endoscopy); octreotide is preferred over vasopressin and terlipressin because it has fewer adverse effects."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Cirrhosis with GI bleeding: antibiotic prophylaxis with ceftriaxone (preferred in advanced cirrhosis, in hospital settings with high prevalence of quinolone-resistant bacterial infections and in patients on previous quinolone prophylaxis); norfloxacin is no longer available in the US; stop a nonselective beta-blocker if there's active hemorrhage with hypotension."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Tranexamic acid may increase banding success and decrease rebleeding in some patients."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Paracentesis > 5 L: give 6-8 g of 25% albumin per liter removed (reduces post-paracentesis hypotension)."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "SBP: albumin 1.5 g/kg on day 1 and 1 g/kg on day 3 reduces hepatorenal syndrome risk and improves survival; hold nonselective beta-blockers if MAP < 65 mm Hg."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
